```gitignore
# =========================
# Unity generated folders
# =========================

[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# Memory captures
[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings
[Rr]ecordings/

# Asset meta data should be committed
# (*.meta files are intentionally NOT ignored)


# =========================
# Unity cache / generated files
# =========================

.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/

# Visual Studio cache
*.csproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj

# Rider
*.sln.iml

# Unity generated solution files
*.csproj
*.unityproj


# =========================
# OS generated files
# =========================

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# macOS
.DS_Store


# =========================
# Crash reports
# =========================

sysinfo.txt


# =========================
# Build artifacts
# =========================

*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage

# Uncomment if you don't want to commit builds
# Builds/
# Build/


# =========================
# Addressables
# =========================

/[ Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*


# =========================
# User-specific settings
# =========================

UserSettings/
```

**Главное:** `Library/`, `Temp/`, `Obj/`, `Logs/` и подобное **не надо коммитить** — Unity сама их генерит.

А вот `Assets/`, `Packages/`, `ProjectSettings/` и `.meta` файлы **обязательно оставляй в Git**, иначе при клонировании проекта будут проблемы.

Для твоего Tower Defense я бы вообще использовал этот `.gitignore` и не заморачивался дальше.
